+## 2. Requirements for Gemini/Vertex failover
+
+1. **One copy of the body**, in the APM's store. Bodies larger than the stream limit stay
+   retriable.
+2. **Every attempt gets byte-identical bytes, or the request is not retried.** Wrong bytes are
+   never sent.
+3. **Each attempt carries only its own cluster's request settings:**
+
+   | Cluster | Path | Credential | Host and SNI |
+   |---|---|---|---|
+   | gemini | `/v1beta/models/{m}:{method}` | `x-goog-api-key` | `generativelanguage.googleapis.com` |
+   | vertex | `/v1/projects/{p}/locations/{l}/publishers/google/models/{m}:{method}` | `Authorization: Bearer` | `{region}-aiplatform.googleapis.com` |
+
+   A request that carries both credentials is expected to be rejected. The mock answers 400
+   "Multiple authentication credentials received", which is Google's error for that case; this
+   was not tried against the live APIs.
+4. **The PDP orders providers per request**, from what the APM parsed, without touching the body.
+5. **Attempt order and count stay in standard config:** `priority_group`,
+   `refresh_cluster_on_retry` and `num_retries`.
+
+## 3. Options
+
+Four independent design passes explored the space: minimal core surface, reliability,
+memory and performance, and long-term generality. Three judges then scored the results.
+
+| Option | Summary | Verdict |
+|---|---|---|
+| A. Router in-memory buffer (today) | Raise `request_body_buffer_limit` | Two copies; raising the limit disables offload. Kept as the fallback when nothing is published |
+| B. Router-owned spool | Router spills its own copy into an `ExternalBuffer` (the earlier revision of this doc) | Safe by construction, but a second store copy next to the APM's, plus a new core extension category and router proto. Follow-up as a second publisher |
+| C. Downstream body source | APM publishes what it emitted; router replays it | One copy, small core contract. The first prototype had integrity holes (section 7) |
+| **C+. Verified borrowed body** | C, but replay only after end-of-body verification, last chunk held, attempt-scoped pacing, shared ownership | **Recommended; all three judges picked it** |
+| D. Per-cluster upstream APM | Upstream APM borrows a router-retained body and renders per attempt | Re-parses per attempt; no watermark fan-out upstream. Gemini/Vertex need no per-provider body |
+| E. Composite or aggregate cluster | One cluster walks sub-clusters | Upstream chain and TLS come from the parent; no per-request order |
+| F. APM-driven failover | APM sends the attempts itself | Re-implements the router; bypasses the PDP and priority_group |
+| G. Upstream APM's own buffer as the retry buffer | Keep it across attempts | Dies with each attempt and receives the replay rather than producing it |
+| H. Spillable HCM body service | Make `buffered_request_data_` spill to a store | Large HCM change; `decodingBuffer()` users expect a synchronous `Buffer::Instance` |
+| I. Hybrid | In-memory below the router limit, borrowed body above it | Never worse than today, but keeps the second copy for small bodies (decision D3) |
+
+Judges' scores (reliability / elegance / core surface / memory / upstream acceptance / fit) for
+C+: 9/7-8/7/7/7/9. The minimal-surface variant of C scored 7/8/8-9/7/8/8-9, but leaves the
+integrity holes open.
+
+## 4. Design (C+)
+
+### 4.1 Overview
+
+```mermaid
+flowchart LR
+  C[client] --> A["APM (downstream)<br/>serve_router_retries"]
+  A -->|offload| EB[("ExternalBuffer<br/>the only copy")]
+  A -->|"emitted body<br/>recorded as spans"| P["ext_proc PDP<br/>header-only"]
+  P --> R["router<br/>priority_group +<br/>refresh_cluster_on_retry"]
+  A -. "publishes (FilterChain)" .-> FS{{"envoy.http.replayable_request_body"}}
+  R -. "CRC32C(received) == CRC32C(published)" .-> FS
+  R -->|"attempt 1: live frames"| G["cluster gemini<br/>lua: Gemini path, drop Bearer<br/>credential: x-goog-api-key<br/>sni: generativelanguage"]
+  FS -->|"retry: ranged reads after verification"| R
+  R -->|"replayed, paced, last chunk held"| V["cluster vertex<br/>lua: Vertex path, drop key<br/>credential: Bearer<br/>sni: aiplatform"]
 ```
 
